## Student Search

**Students → Student Search** lists every student in a table you can search, filter and sort. It is
built for questions like "which students have no guardian phone number?" as much as for finding one
person.

- **Search** takes a name, ID, class, guardian or phone number. Use **Search By** to restrict it to
  one field, for example RFID or Address; *All fields* is the default.
- **Class** and **Gender** filters narrow the list.
- **Missing** shows students with a blank value in one field: **Mobile**, **Parent / Guardian**,
  **Address**, **Email**, **Date of Birth**, **Religion**, **Nationality** or **RFID**. It is the quickest
  way to find records that need fixing, for example before issuing
  [ID cards](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-id-cards).
- **Reset Filters** appears once any filter is active.
- Click a column header to sort. **Columns** hides or shows columns, and **Compact** / **Comfortable**
  changes how tightly rows are packed.

*No students match your search.* means exactly that; clear a filter before assuming the student is
missing. To pull the same data out as a file, see [List Reports](/docs/educonnect-list-reports).

## The student profile

Select a student to open their profile. The header stays in place while you scroll through the
sections, and after you edit and save you stay on the profile with the saved values showing. Student
lists across the app, including the mobile list, show each student's photo where there is one.

Attendance appears in two forms:

- **Term Attendance** — the term's attendance summary.
- **Attendance by Day** — a calendar grid for the term you pick from the **Term 1, Term 2…**
  dropdown, one cell per day, coloured **Present**, **Absent**, **Not a school day** or **Upcoming**.
  Below it, a chip counts school days attended, for example *18 / 20 school days attended (90.0%)*,
  or says *No school days held yet*.

Not-a-school-day cells come from your [Calendar](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-holidays-and-terms)
(weekends, holidays and days outside term), so an absence you see on a holiday means the holiday
isn't configured.

Further down are exam results, payments, certificates, siblings and previous classes. Students with a
card on record also show an **ID Card** section (see
[Manage and Track ID Cards](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-id-cards)).

### Permanent Record

If your institute has turned it on, the **Permanent Record** section holds dated notes in the
categories **Conduct**, **Academic**, **Health** and **Other**. Select **Add entry**, choose a category
and date, write the note, and save. Each entry shows who added it (and who edited it).

It is off until an administrator switches on **Enable the permanent record section** in
**Administration → Settings**. Only teachers and administrators can read it, never parents. Teachers can
add and edit entries for their own class; only administrators can delete. Turning the setting off
hides the section but keeps the entries.

## When a student leaves

Someone with the *Mark students as left school* permission (set in Access Control) takes a student off the roll
from the student's edit page with the **Mark as left** button. The dialog asks for the **Date left**, a **Reason** and an optional
**Note**. Reasons are:
*Finished school*, *Moved to a different school*, *Relocated abroad*, *Financial reasons*, *Family
reasons* and *Other*. You will see *Student marked as left school*.

**Students → Left Students** lists everyone marked as left, with their ID, last attended class, date
joined, date left and reason. Search by name, student ID or class, and sort by any of those columns.
A student in the deleted records can be moved on to this list with **Move to left students**.
Deleted students keep a profile that still loads from those records.

Left students are not counted in the roll or in admissions figures; see
[School Statistics](/docs/shared-staff-analytics).

